eading?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=short&passage=density-consequence","ref":"sha256:bc21296455ab786301336177a360e9aca944f4a42bbefc6e55b5b9c49382c6bd/papers/short.md/sha256:367dea1089c1066db4783d23742fcf2967eb6489ced82d2f7c87fecaab08f43b/papers/short.json/passages/density-consequence","section_ref":"sha256:bc21296455ab786301336177a360e9aca944f4a42bbefc6e55b5b9c49382c6bd/papers/short.md/sections/29484","section_title":"4. Strict positivity of the density","stage":"short","treatments":[{"claim_id":"scalar.smooth_positive_density","claim_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Develops smoothness from the quotient of moments before differentiating, then transfers the quantitative spatial-moment inequality through local constant replacements at a fixed interior time. Compact-strip stability is a cited input; positivity is asserted only for 0<t<1, and the argument does not transfer third time derivatives or add formal acceptance."},{"claim_id":"support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","claim_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","kinds":["derivation","explanation"],"rationale":"Derives the continuous-coefficient fixed-time inequality by admissible local constant replacement and common-strip convergence of spatial moments, then applies it after q=t. Minimality is unnecessary for the transfer itself."}]},{"anchor":"density-and-approximation","claim_refs":["sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density"],"content_span":{"end_byte":60781,"end_line":1431,"start_byte":60042,"start_line":1422},"evidence_class":"source_argument","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=expository&passage=density-and-app